    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Governor Jared Polis is a different kind of politician, governing a different kind of state, a sweeping mountainous oasis. Colorado is an increasingly popular and populous state, while Polis is a libertarian technocrat who plays video games and takes in the MLB's Colorado Rockies games to de-stress. all the while retaining a popular fan base himself over two terms in office. Most of all, Governor Polis has promoted Colorado's identity as a pro-liberty state that protects bodily autonomy, whether that's access to abortion, weed, porn, technology, or industrial ventures. The Governor has also been on a mission to put Pueblo, Colorado on the map, along with the higher profile destinations like Aspen, Denver, and Colorado Springs. Governor Poliss and I met at fuel and iron, Pueblo's first ever modern food hall, where his administration is helping revitalize what he considers an unsung heart of the state. Both being foodies, we tried everything from hot chicken and roast beef to ramen noodles and ice cream. The governor and I talked about fatherhood, electric vehicles, and both the housing crisis and opportunity in a state to which millions have flocked in recent years. Also on the agenda, baseball season, the NBA champion Denver Nuggets, Vladimir Putin, and Elon Musk. So we're here in Puebla at Fuel and Iron, an establishment that just arose. What made you want to restore and revive Puebla?",
