    "turn_idx": 68,
    "turn_text": "Our last few governors have all been, I guess, relatively young in the scheme of governors, so they've all had, like, young families. Governor Hickenlooper raised his son who's now 19 or so while he was governor, Governor Ritter, several kids, Governor Owens, kids. I think the last older governor we had would have been Governor Romer, who, when he started, his kids were still with him, too, and then they grew up. He was governor before tournament, so he was there for 12 years. So it's hard to do both, but our state also, I think, values kind of people that are facing the same kind of family experience that others are facing. And, you know, we try to keep some degree of separation, the capitals in Denver, but our families in Boulder. And that's where we've always lived. We didn't move to Denver. But no, it's great. Our kids are great. And as I said, our daughter's doing baseball or something likes to cook and we're having fun with it. I testified before the house education and workforce committee are now controlled by Republicans a few months ago. I don't want to the Republicans there. They've somehow thought they were getting me. They're like, I hear, you know, that you're the You know father of an eight year old girl how do you feel if if she was on you know there were boys on her team You know one of these things like they're going after transgender I said well there are she's co it's using coed little league I don't know like what's the what's the big deal like the other little league is coed like I don't I don't understand what you're talking about",
