    "turn_text": "I think it's easier than some people think. I mean, say what you're going to do and do it is one big thing that I focus on. I said I was going to do in the campaign and I worked hard to do it. succeeded in some and maybe didn't get others done, but I just did what I said I was going to do. And then the other maximum I liked to use is that if it was easy it would have been done already. It doesn't take a governor or a leader to get something done that's easy. It just happens. It takes taking on the big challenges. In our state it was things like how do we fund our rows. Now we're dealing with housing affordability is a big thing. These are not easy things. They went unsolved for many years. The default is for them to be unsolved. or a leader or a governor can pull together a coalition to get it done and she was a course of history. Right. Our ice cream is melting and this brownie is just.",
